ruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":-0.0075,"r5":0.0383,"r20":-0.0032,"r1_spy":0.0043,"r5_spy":0.0393,"r20_spy":0.0523}}],"quotes":[{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"James Hoffman","x":"Lead time still remain extended and scrap pricing is solid as a result of the healthy demand and ongoing section 232 activity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"William Sales","x":"Our average selling prices for stainless steel products also increased, mainly as a result of the price increase -- increases announced by the mills related to Section 232 actions in rising input costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Gregg Mollins","x":"Given multiple price increases in 2018, we followed our normal practice and passed through higher metal prices prior to receiving the higher cost metal into our inventory, which positively impacted our FIFO gross profit margin.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Gregg Mollins","x":"So far in the fourth quarter prices have generally remained steady to positive, which we expect to continue throughout the remainder of the year, especially in light of rising scrap costs and price increases for carbon flat-rolled products announced earlier this month.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Gregg Mollins","x":"Our pre-tax impairment and restructuring charges of $36.8 million for the quarter included costs related to this downsizing, as well as the restructuring of a few of our smaller locations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2018-10-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Karla Lewis","x":"So the bulk of that impairment restructuring charge did relate to downsizing the one energy business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/25/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2018-earnings-con.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2019-02-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"Our fourth quarter pricing outlook of flat to up 1% factor in the potential for some price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/21/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2018-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2018 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2019-02-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"Following the October announcement of a price increase for carbon flat-rolled products which did not hold.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/21/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2018-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2019-04-25","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Timna Tanners","x":"And then on the beam side, if you can discuss the impact, if any, yet on the preliminary tariffs on the imported fabricated beams, which we've heard is kind of a big deal.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2019-04-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"However, our average selling price in the first quarter increased 13.6% compared to the first quarter of 2018, supported by multiple mill price increases throughout 2018 relatively steady demand and the effects of ongoing trade actions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2019-04-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"As for pricing, mill pricing for carbon steel products remained at high levels in the first quarter following multiple price increases throughout 2018, but softened somewhat compared to the prior quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2019-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"Compared to the second quarter of 2018, our tons sold declined 4.9%, however, we do not believe the decline in shipments is reflective of end demand as there was unusual buying activity in the second quarter of 2018 due to the enactment of Section 232 tariffs at that time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2019-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Hunter Alley","x":"How should we think about the removal of Section 232 tariffs on Canada, Mexico impacting Reliance?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2019-07-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"…market consist of heat-treated aluminum products, primarily plate and as well as specialty stainless steel and titanium products, given strong demand environment, the recently announced 5% price increase on heat-treated aluminum plate effective in August has been fully supported by the market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2019-07-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"Also given that carbon steel prices appear to have bottomed with potential for mill price increases in certain products, we expect our FIFO gross profit margin to remain consistent with levels achieved so far in 2019.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/25/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2019-10-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James Hoffman","x":"At the time we provided third quarter guidance, multiple mill price increases had been announced for certain carbon steel products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/24/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2019-10-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James Hoffman","x":"The 5% mill price increase on heat-treated aluminum plate, which became effective in August and has full market support benefited our third quarter sales into the aerospace market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/24/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2019-10-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Karla Lewis","x":"Net income attributable to Reliance for the third quarter of 2019 was $162.7 million or $2.40 per diluted share compared to $148.3 million or $2.03 in the third quarter of 2018, which included a $36.8 million impairment and restructuring charge.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/24/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2019-10-24","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Hoffman","x":"We look at our headcount, we look at our expenses and if we think it's going to be -- continue to be weak, we call it right-sizing, whether it's an head count or inventory control or whatever, it's the same thing we've been doing for a long period of time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/24/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2020-02-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"For the full year 2019, we recorded LIFO income of $156 million compared to LIFO expense of $271.8 million in 2018 when metal prices rose throughout the year, mainly due to Section 232.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2020-02-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"…throughout 2019 that at Reliance, along with, we believe, many other service centers during 2018, when Section 232 was announced, there was a bit of a run, so to speak, on buying and so we bought a little heavier than we maybe needed to for where demand ended up throughout the remainder of 2018.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2020-02-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"Our focus on rightsizing our inventory, improved our inventory turn rate to 4.5 times in 2019 from 4.2 times in 2018, approaching our companywide goal of 4.7 times.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2019 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2020-02-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"We saw it coming, we decided to get our inventory in line, which we have tended to always do, headcount reduction.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/20/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2020-04-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"We have taken difficult action, including workforce reduction, to right size our operations to sustainable levels that we believe will enable us to emerge from this current crisis intact, prepared and positioned to face new business realities, including the ability to quickly ramp up with our…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/23/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2020-04-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"…instance, during the Great Recession when our 2009 shipments fell 32% and our average selling price declined 18.4% from 2008, we took immediate action including reducing our workforce by 21% and lowering inventory by over $1 billion in a nine-month period from September 2008 through June of 2009.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/23/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"As about 65% of our SG&A expenses are people related, we reduced our workforce through temporary layoffs and permanent reductions in force impacting a total of approximately 2,100 employees by mid-July.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2020-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"If we see further changes in shipment activities, we will take additional action to right-size our workforce.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/23/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2020-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"Metal pricing began to improve in the third quarter as mill price increases from many of the products we sell were implemented, with announcements for further price increases continuing into the fourth quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2020-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"Despite these mill price increases, our average selling price per ton sold in the third quarter was down 4.3% compared to the second quarter, primarily as a result of product mix changes that Karla will discuss in more detail.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2020-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"…to reduced commercial airline build rates that we expect to continue at low levels in the near term, we recorded impairment and restructuring charges related to facility closures, workforce reductions and a negative outlook at certain of our businesses servicing the commercial aerospace market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2020-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"We will continue to monitor and assess the health of each of our aerospace businesses and take appropriate cost-reduction actions, if and when needed, to ensure the continued long-term profitability of these businesses.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2021-02-18","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"Supported by solid demand and rising input costs, metal pricing improved as mill price increases for many of the products we sell accelerated throughout the fourth quarter with prices for certain carbon steel products almost doubling, which led to our average selling price increasing 4.6%…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2021-02-18","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"…reflects the outstanding performance by our managers in the field who effectively implemented price increases at the time of mill announcement prior to receiving the higher-cost metal into inventory, pushing our gross profit margin above already strong levels, resulting from our focus on…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2021-02-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"Fueled by our ongoing focus on rightsizing our inventory to reflect current demand levels and our differentiating advantage of cross-selling inventory among our family of companies, we achieved our companywide inventory turn goal of 4.7 times based on tons for 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2020 Q4","e":"rs","d":"2021-02-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"And throughout 2020, we took prudent cost-reduction measures, including the closure of certain facilities, which helped strengthen our overall efficiency and position us to support a recovery in this market.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2021-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"We experienced ongoing strength in metals pricing during the first quarter, led by multiple price increases for carbon steel products, along with improving demand in many markets, and leveraged our decentralized operating structure, small order sizes and diversification of products, end markets…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2021-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"…of outstanding execution by our managers in the field who once again effectively implemented price increases at the time of mill announcement prior to receiving the higher-cost metal into inventory, maintained their focus on higher-margin orders and were very selective given limited metal…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/22/reliance-steel-and-aluminum-co-rs-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2021-07-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"During the second quarter, we continued to experience considerable strength in metals pricing led by multiple mill price increases for carbon and stainless steel products in particular.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/22/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2021-07-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"We're not saying at the same rate that we saw price increases on some of those products earlier in 2021, but we see prices holding not any individual items that we're thinking we're going to see certainly any material decline in prices.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/22/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2021-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"James D. Hoffman","x":"The trends of strengthening metals pricing persisted through the third quarter, which featured multiple mill price increases, most notably for carbon and stainless steel products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/28/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"RS 2021 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2021-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"…effort, relentless focus on high-quality, high-margin business and effective implementation of price increases at the time of no announcement, which enabled us to capture an incremental margin benefit in excess of already strong levels, and further supporting these efforts, with the enhanced…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/28/reliance-steel-aluminum-co-rs-q3-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2025-07-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen P. Koch","x":"Our second quarter tons sold decreased 0.9% compared to the first quarter of 2025 in line with our outlook of down 1% to up 1%, even when considering the effect of demand pull forward into Q1 due to tariff activity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2025-07-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen P. Koch","x":"Our second quarter average selling price per ton sold increased 6.1% compared to the first quarter of 2025, doubling the high end of our expected range of up 1% to 3%, reflecting the strong tariff-driven momentum for both demand and pricing near the end of the first quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2025-07-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"If you recall at the end of Q1, we talked about some potential demand pull forward into Q1 and there were price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q2","e":"rs","d":"2025-07-24","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"So we -- and we expect that to continue to flow through in Q3 as well as a base price increase on stainless near the end of Q2.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q2-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2025-10-23","l":"ai_spend","r":"analyst","s":"Martin Englert","x":"I'm curious, how much of this activity do you think is related tied to AI, data centers, semiconductor build-outs, kind of that camp of activity?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2025-10-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Koch","x":"Consistent with our outlook, our third quarter average selling price remained steady compared to the second quarter of 2025, even as tariff-related momentum quickly leveled off.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2025-10-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Koch","x":"Through industry overbuying in the first quarter of this year in advance of the tariffs as well as readily available inventory at domestic mills and depots, pricing for most products has been declining since April, resulting in a very competitive market, which, when combined with stable to…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2025-10-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Karla Lewis","x":"In this environment, it is more difficult to immediately increase selling prices to fully offset mill price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2025 Q3","e":"rs","d":"2025-10-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Arthur Ajemyan","x":"Tariffs initially drove rapid price increases for carbon steel products, which slightly elevated carbon steel margins.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/reliance-rs-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2026 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2026-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Karla R. Lewis","x":"Our first quarter tons sold were a record and were up both sequentially and year over year, a result that is especially notable given the unusually strong tariff-driven demand pull-forward in the prior-year period.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/reliance-rs-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2026 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2026-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Arthur Ajemyan","x":"I would like to also briefly address the impact of incremental Section 232 tariffs on our gross profit margins and profitability.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/reliance-rs-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2026 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2026-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Arthur Ajemyan","x":"Our pricing discipline enabled us to pass through higher mill pricing on most product in the first quarter and expand margins.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/reliance-rs-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"RS 2026 Q1","e":"rs","d":"2026-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Arthur Ajemyan","x":"So on the guide for Q2 around gross profit margin, which we do not explicitly provide guidance on, Q1 was a good strong pricing environment with a lot of products having price increases, which gives us an opportunity to drive our margins up a bit for a temporary period.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/reliance-rs-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1,5790,0,0,0,5060,393],[36,1,9307,0,0,0,7464,1341],[37,1,5873,0,0,0,4465,1000],[38,1,5281,0,0,0,4649,354],[39,1,6741,0,0,0,5715,711],[40,1,7985,0,0,0,5984,1647],[41,1,9770,0,0,0,8277,1108],[42,1,7306,0,0,0,6222,753],[43,1,10561,0,0,0,8547,1480],[44,1,5422,0,0,0,4362,846],[45,1,6756,0,0,0,5806,652],[46,1,7016,0,0,0,5974,706],[47,1,8068,0,0,0,6764,920],[62,1,4717,0,0,0,4008,508],[63,1,7148,0,0,0,5833,1049],[65,1,4186,0,0,0,3298,691],[67,1,5015,0,0,0,3902,835]],"cinema":[[35,1,5790,0,0,0,5060,393],[36,1,9307,0,0,0,7464,1341],[37